MCHL: Now, about the prototype. You led the mission to steal it yourself, yes? They deployed you straight out of debriefing from the infiltration? If you'd had more time, would you have talked to... (RUSTLE OF PAPERS) Corporal Baker?

RBTS: The Soviets had a superweapon hanging over our heads and we had the chance to stop it ever being finished - maybe even finish it ourselves. Of course I deployed straight out of debriefing, I'd have stayed out in the field if I could. The hell does Baker have to do with any of this?

MCHL: Corporal Baker's technical expertise was enough to identify several key aspects of the Mammoth's design and the technology it is based on that had previously eluded our own research staff and may go some way to explaining how the CCA were able to develop it without our knowledge.

RBTS: (SOTTO VOCE) The scientist the traitors were working with might have had something to do with that.

MCHL: Stealing the prototype - could that have been the plan all along?

RBTS: We all wanted that thing gone for good. Why could Shaw have wanted to steal it?

MCHL: I don't know, Lieutenant. Why could Shaw have wanted to steal it?